Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.43,0:00:05.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Before meeting the qubit let's begin with a familiar\Nidea the bit A bit can have the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.19,0:00:10.68,Default,,0,0,0,,value zero or the value one We can imagine a switch off\Nrepresents zero and on represents
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.69,0:00:15.71,Default,,0,0,0,,one This comparison helps us understand information but\Na real computer can represent
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.72,0:00:20.87,Default,,0,0,0,,these values in other ways such as different electrical\Nvoltages Pictures messages and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.88,0:00:25.43,Default,,0,0,0,,games are stored using enormous collections of bits By\Nfollowing rules that transform
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.44,0:00:30.97,Default,,0,0,0,,this information computers perform calculations Our\Nexplorer asks a simple question what
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.98,0:00:33.72,Default,,0,0,0,,if nature allowed us to transform information in a\Ndifferent way